  "term": "ciliary body",
  "definition": "The ciliary body is a ring-shaped tissue in the eye that runs from the scleral spur to the ora serrata of the retina. It has a uveal part, which contains the ciliary muscle, and an epithelial part, which contains the ciliary processes.",
